+# Full render-options NAP profiles (2026-10-19)
+
+Two Release client (`19edc4a-git`) runs explicitly enabled the current renderer options, `--invulnerable=on`, and `--render-profile-capture=on`. Both loaded game data and UI, entered the moving M01A/FP7 intro mission, and wrote exactly 300 CSV frames. Each CSV's `render_options_initial_json` confirms HDR, bloom, depth prepass, shadows, SSAO, soft particles, normal maps, surface PBR maps, PBR environment maps, diffuse IBL, colored sun ambient, dynamic lights, and effect toggles were active. SMAA High and anisotropy 16 were requested.
+
+An exploratory third run kept the same settings except normal maps, surface PBR maps, PBR environment maps, and diffuse IBL were disabled. It is not a controlled A/B: mission timing, camera, NPCs, effects, shader warm-up, and simulation load kept changing. Its result also reverses the first apparent FPS difference, so it cannot establish the cost of those features.
+
+## Run conditions
+
+- GPU: Intel HD Graphics 4600 (Haswell GT2), Mesa 23.2.1, OpenGL 4.6
+- Resolution: 1280×720; VSync off; Release client; no debug overlay
+- Active package set: `lancer-profile-counters-20261019`, 13 NAPs
+- Provenance: package inputs came only from `Data/NAP/.runtime-test-stage/package-inputs-20261016/`; each archive passed `nexus-pack verify`, and active-manifest sizes and SHA-256 hashes matched. No loose `DATA` directory was present.
+- All three runs reached `Finished loading game data`, `Interface loaded`, and `Profile: Saved 300 frames`.
+
+The table summarizes the **last 150 captured frames** to avoid presenting initial setup spikes as steady behavior. This is still moving gameplay, not a repeatable benchmark.
+
+| Settings | FPS p50 | Frame interval p50 / p95 | CPU update+draw p50 / p95 | Opaque GPU pass p50 / p95 | Dropped simulation ticks total |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| Full options, run 1 | 40.04 | 24.980 / 35.060 ms | 10.503 / 15.754 ms | 5.531 / 16.153 ms | 467 |
+| Maps/IBL disabled | 47.56 | 21.028 / 28.101 ms | 9.190 / 13.919 ms | 3.711 / 10.485 ms | 356 |
+| Full options, repeat | 52.80 | 18.941 / 23.757 ms | 11.797 / 18.547 ms | 4.766 / 10.770 ms | 355 |
+
+The full-options repeat is faster by median FPS than the maps-disabled run, while its CPU update+draw median is slower. That inconsistency demonstrates that simulation and scene variation are large enough to swamp this exploratory comparison. The asynchronous GPU timer-query samples also have delayed/old-sample ages; their p95/max values are not frame-aligned costs to sum.
+
+## Interpretation and limits
+
+These runs prove that the combined current OpenGL renderer path can load and render with the full option set on this Intel iGPU. They also show that one Intel HD 4600 profile can sit near 40–53 FPS median under the moving M01A intro workload, with hundreds of dropped simulation ticks. They do not prove visual correctness of each feature, isolate individual costs, establish a stable baseline, or predict RTX 5060 performance. Before choosing an optimization, capture repeatable fixed-camera scenes and compare at least three runs per option state on the target GPU.
+
+Existing data warnings (unknown INI fields, duplicate entries, missing string IDs, incomplete placeholder `sun.sph`) appeared without preventing these captures. They are separate compatibility/content issues.
+
+Artifacts: [`frame-profile.csv`](frame-profile.csv), [`frame-profile-repeat.csv`](frame-profile-repeat.csv), [`frame-profile-maps-disabled.csv`](frame-profile-maps-disabled.csv), [`active-manifest.json`](active-manifest.json), [`runtime-evidence.log.txt`](runtime-evidence.log.txt), [`launch-options.txt`](launch-options.txt), and [`maps-disabled-options.txt`](maps-disabled-options.txt).
